TI  - AIOpsLab in Action: An Open Platform for AIOps Research
AU  - Ma, Minghua
AU  - Clark, Jackson
AU  - Zhang, Shenglin
T3  - FSE Companion '25
AB  - The significant advances in AI have been driving a blooming landscape of research on developing AI agents for various kinds of cloud system operations, which is often referred to as AIOps. For example, AI-based fault detection, root cause analysis, and failure mitigation have been a hot topic in recent years with many research papers published at Software Engineering conferences like FSE, ICSE, ASE, and ISSTA. However, AIOps research today faces major practical challenges such as benchmarking, workload simulation, and reproducibility.This tutorial introduces AIOpsLab, an open platform and benchmark suites designed with the goal of significantly boosting the design, implementation, and evaluation of AI agents for cloud system operations. Specifically, AIOpsLab addresses following needs:• Standard benchmark suites for evaluating AIOps techniques comprehensively and fairly;• A usable platform with push-button deployment to let researchers focus on the essence of AIOps research and development;• An extensible framework that can be easily enriched and customized for different AIOps tasks and scenarios;• Reproducibility of the research results and artifacts.Specifically, we will cover the following topics in the tutorial:• The vision and objectives of AIOpsLab;• The design and implementation of AIOpsLab;• The use cases of AIOpsLab with a hands-on session;• The benchmark suites in AIOpsLab and how to extend them;• The design of a fault localization agent and the results obtained using AIOpsLab;• A discussion on next steps and future endeavors of AIOpsLab.The source code, blog, and additional resources for AIOpsLab are available at https://aka.ms/aiopslab.
