AB  - Artificial Intelligence and Cloud computing are often used together for implementing automated tasks, that is, activities that execute without or with limited human supervision. Automated tasks range from pure software activities such automated cloud operations (also known as AIOps), to tasks that include mechanical or/and electrical systems (also known as Cyber Physical Systems and Internet of Things). Automation is based on feedback loops, made of services such as collection and aggregation of data from the system to be automated and from the environment in which it operates; identification of events, such as anomalies, trends and patterns related to system operation or to the environment; identification, planning and execution of remediation steps. This workshop brought together researchers and practitioners to present and discuss the state of the art and practice in AI, Cloud and Automation, to identify challenges and opportunities for further research and commercialization. The workshop agenda consisted of industrial talks that presented the state of the practice; research talks that presented current research projects; and a round table that discussed the research challenges and opportunities.
